# Attraction page

Read `.cursor/skills/attraction-page/SKILL.md` before drafting or restyling an attraction.

- A lede, one photo, and a fact bar are a stub. A finished page has a kicker, body, a second photo, getting there, and hours and fees.
- Do not invent a fee, an hour, a drive time, or a coordinate. Unknowns stay “Check on arrival”.
- Do not add review counts, visitor ranks, ads, a map iframe, or a booking form.
- Open the photo and look at it. Keep a frame where the sight reads in one glance. Reject a gray frame where the subject does not.
- The reference record is `src/content/attractions/da-nang--ba-na.json`. Copy its shape, not its sentences.
